  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="work" n="6">
        <pb n="143"/>
        <head>The Suffrages of <persName>Mar Balai</persName></head>
        <head>Another.<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a1" target="#n1" n="1"/></head>
        <lg n="6.1">
          <l n="1"><persName>Our Lord</persName> in the upper room</l>
          <l n="2">Commanded His Disciples:</l>
          <l n="3"><quote>Be ye assembling together</quote></l>
          <l n="4"><quote>And keeping My memorial,</quote>—</l>
          <l n="5">Until His second coming</l>
          <l n="6">In the Resurrection.</l>
        </lg>
        <lg n="6.2">
          <l n="7">Plain it is to the discerning,</l>
          <l n="8">That the departed are profited</l>
          <l n="9">By vigils and oblations,</l>
          <l n="10">And the thuribles of propitiation.</l>
        </lg>
        <lg n="6.3">
          <l n="11">That he makes mention of their names,—</l>
          <l n="12">Even the priest before the Altar,—</l>
          <l n="13">Those on high rejoice,</l>
          <l n="14">And those beneath are glad.</l>
          <l n="15">The dead exult,</l>
          <l n="16">To whom we call this day</l>
          <l n="17">That they may delight</l>
          <l n="18">In the heavenly Sacrifice.</l>
        </lg>
        <lg n="6.4">
          <l n="19">Glory to the Living One,</l>
          <l n="20">Who raised them up by His Death,</l>
          <l n="21">And made for them a hope,—</l>
          <l n="22">Even for the dead,—in the Resurrection!</l>
          <l n="23">And He will come and raise them up;</l>
          <l n="24">And they shall sing praises (to Him).</l>
        </lg>
      </div>
      <noteGrp>
        <note xml:id="n1" target="#a1" n="1"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 143, n. 1</orig></choice> This hymn and the next are evidently about the departed, though they have no description attached.</note>
      </noteGrp>
    </body>
